1
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:20,770
Steps for labeling a diagram.

2
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:23,150
The first step is to look at the

3
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:25,670
diagram to identify what it describes.

4
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:29,390
For example, some questions require you to label

5
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:30,290
a water filter.

6
00:00:31,049 --> 00:00:33,170
In step 2, you have to predict the suitable 

7
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:34,870
information for each blank.

8
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:37,830
If the question's requirement is to fill in

9
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:40,090
words on the diagram, then you should pay

10
00:00:40,090 --> 00:00:41,270
attention to the word limit.

11
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:44,070
In step 3, you have to listen and

12
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:45,390
fill in the correct answers.

13
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:48,270
In case you get lost, take notes immediately

14
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:49,950
and do not panic.

15
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:53,850
In step 4, after listening, you should check

16
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:56,090
your answers and never leave your answer sheet

17
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:56,510
blank.

18
00:00:57,110 --> 00:00:59,070
Let's look at an example together.

19
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:01,450
In this exercise, you will listen to two

20
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:03,970
students discussing a lecture that one of them

21
00:01:03,970 --> 00:01:04,570
had missed.

22
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:06,930
From the name of the diagram, you can tell 

23
00:01:06,930 --> 00:01:09,110
that the recording talks about the formation

24
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:12,070
of meteoroid, meteor and meteorite.

25
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:15,450
With this type, we don't have given options, so 

26
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:17,090
we have to fill in the correct

27
00:01:17,090 --> 00:01:17,550
answers.

28
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:20,530
The word limit is to write one word

29
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:21,110
only.

30
00:01:22,130 --> 00:01:22,650
Step 2.

31
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:25,590
Predict the information in each blank.

32
00:01:26,230 --> 00:01:30,890
For example, blank number 1 needs a noun

33
00:01:30,890 --> 00:01:33,610
referring to something around the sun.

34
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:37,670
Blank number 2 needs a noun referring to

35
00:01:37,670 --> 00:01:39,690
something on or around here.

36
00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:43,350
And blank number 3 also needs a noun

37
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:46,110
referring to something in the space environment.

38
00:01:46,650 --> 00:01:48,130
As you can see, it is an area

39
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:49,930
between Earth and space.

40
00:01:50,690 --> 00:01:52,890
Now, you will listen to the recording and

41
00:01:52,890 --> 00:01:54,870
fill in this diagram in the practice section.

42
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:55,830
Let's go!

